    {
      "index": 2,
      "id": "3899048680142491945_77766",
      "question": "The Red Fort was the imperial residence for rulers of this empire that was established after victory at the First Battle of Panipat.\nFor the point, identify this Indian empire founded by Babur and once ruled by Akbar the Great.",
      "meta": {
        "category": "South Asia",
        "era": "04",
        "source": "original"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "id": "4124515485880797130_77766",
      "question": "\" For several years, this illegitimate daughter of Lord Byron corresponded with Charles Babbage and helped him refine his invention, which was then known as a \"difference engine.\n\" For the point, name this woman, arguably the first computer programmer.",
      "meta": {
        "category": "Europe",
        "era": "05",
        "source": "original"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "id": "nonteam_more_023",
      "question": "Hiram Bingham brought international attention to it after reaching its terraces in 1911.\nFor the point, name this Inca citadel high in the Andes.",
      "meta": {
        "category": "Latin America",
        "era": "04",
        "source": "original"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "id": "nonteam_more_041",
      "question": "She was later captured, tried for heresy, and burned at Rouen before being canonized centuries later.\nFor the point, name this French saint nicknamed the Maid of Orleans.",
      "meta": {
        "category": "Europe",
        "era": "03",
        "source": "original"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "id": "team_more_049",
      "question": "Its Templo Mayor stood near markets and palaces before Spanish forces destroyed it in 1521.\nFor the point, name this Aztec capital later replaced by Mexico City.",
      "meta": {
        "category": "Latin America",
        "era": "04",
        "source": "original"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "id": "team_more_080",
      "question": "Marco Polo claimed to have visited its court at Dadu.\nFor the point, name this Mongol-led dynasty of China.",
      "meta": {
        "category": "East Asia",
        "era": "03",
        "source": "original"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "id": "2582061108731926815_77766",
      "question": "This man authorized the use of toxic gas during the Battle of Wuhan and cited the Five Charter Oath while denouncing his divinity in the Humanity Declaration.\nPrime Minister Hideki Tojo served, for the point, what emperor who delivered the Jewel Voice Broadcast and led Japan during World War Two?",
      "meta": {
        "category": "East Asia",
        "era": "06",
        "source": "original"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "id": "nonteam_more_066",
      "question": "It ended in 1945 after Germany surrendered and atomic bombs were dropped on Japan.\nFor the point, name this global conflict between the Allies and Axis.",
      "meta": {
        "category": "World",
        "era": "06",
        "source": "original"
      }
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "id": "nonteam_more_014",
      "question": "It defeated a British force at Isandlwana before losing later in 1879.\nFor the point, name this southern African kingdom.",
      "meta": {
